# The package description for tools/package.py (NBTFoundry/manager): one argument
# per line. `make package` and the release workflow both use it; they add the
# version, sequence, key, output and executable. Bridge 1.7: the payload is a
# module built without the QNX SDP, run by NBT Manager's nbt-runner (runner);
# the games come through `files`.
--app
snes9x
--compat
nbt_6.5_armv7
--bridge
1.7
--bridge-uses
show,controller,files,runner
--bridge-optional
status,live-settings,gamepad
--bridge-files
sfc,smc,fig,swc|16|1024
--setting
aspect|Aspect|4-3|4-3,pixel,full
--setting
filter|Filter|sharp|sharp,smooth,nearest
--setting
region|Region|auto|auto,ntsc,pal
--setting
frameskip|Frame skip|off|off,auto,1,2
--setting
sound|Sound|on|on,off
--setting
show_fps|Show FPS|off|off,on
--setting
debug_log|Debug log|off|off,on
# What the phone app shows before an install (NBT Manager's PROTOCOL.md,
# "Package information"): the Snes9x version the pin builds
# (tools/package_version.py: `make package-args`; `make test` checks it), the
# project, the licence and the notices.
--property
Snes9x|1.63
--property
Project|Snes9x (https://github.com/snes9xgit/snes9x)
--property
Licence|Snes9x licence (non-commercial)
--text
Super Nintendo games by Snes9x, with NBTFoundry's changes for NBT Manager.
--text=
--text
Snes9x may be used and shared for non-commercial purposes only. No game is included.
--text=
--text
Source, licences and notices: https://github.com/NBTFoundry/nf-snes9x
